      "structure_description": "The discrete {Gd12Na6} cage is a quadruple-wheel comprising two {Gd6} rings between two {Na3} triangles. The Gd rings form a distorted hexagonal prism and the Na triangles a trigonal antiprism. Acetate, formate, and carbonate ligands link the rings; six carbonate-centered, edge-sharing {Gd4Na} pentagons provide an alternative description of the metallic core."
